cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PyConformal Engine"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself
  and the underlying thesis listed in the `references` field.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vega Penagos"
    given-names: "Cesar A"
    affiliation: "N/A"
    # email: replace_me@example.com
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cavegap/pyconformal-engine"
url: "https://cavegap.github.io/pyconformal-engine/"
abstract: >-
  PyConformal Engine is a Python library for conformal mappings,
  implementing the mathematical content of the undergraduate thesis
  "Implementación en software de aplicaciones conformes" (Vega Penagos
  & Olivero Zapata, Universidad del Tolima, 2015) as a numerical,
  open-source replacement for the original Maple 17 implementation.
  The library covers angle-preserving linear transformations (group P),
  holomorphic and antiholomorphic maps, Möbius transformations,
  elementary and trigonometric mappings, and the Schwarz-Christoffel
  transformation. The flagship example is the Mercator-style projection
  of the lunar surface described in Chapter 4 of the thesis.
keywords:
  - conformal mapping
  - complex analysis
  - Schwarz-Christoffel
  - Möbius transformation
  - scientific computing
  - cartographic projection
license: MIT
version: "0.0.1"
date-released: "2026-01-01"
